  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 1215 AM MDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nTomorrow, it heats up once again and 100s will be common over the \nplains by afternoon. Any precip that does form will be down along \nthe immediate NM border region, especially the southern Sangre De \nCristo mtns. A fire weather watch has been issued for the Pueblo and \nFremont county regions this day as gap flow winds and RH values will \nreach marginal critical values. \n\nFor Saturday, hot and dry. Max temps plains will continue to \nwarm up with readings 95 to 105, and Low 90s in the valleys. \nCritical fire weather conditions may develop over the far \neastern plains on this day.\n\nSunday will be nearly identical to Saturday, although we should \nstart to see an uptick in showers over the mtns, especially along \nthe Divide, and monsoon moisture starts to push northward once again.\n\nMonday, we begin to SLOWLY cool down and moisture will also slowly \nincrease across the region, especially over the mtns. We may see \nsome showers push out onto the plains Monday evening. \n\nFrom Tuesday onward, temperatures will continue to cool down each \nday with better moisture moving into the region. By mid to late week \nwe may have to start worrying about monsoon flooding returning to \nthe region, especially THU and FRI. Temps by late in the week may \nonly be in the 80s plains and valleys. \\/Hodanish",
